the once green hills of marmaris have  turned into this hectares of scorched  land  and smoke everywhere as firefighting  helicopters  douse the flames the fires here are  mostly contained now but  the damage they left behind is immense  in antalya's manav gut district this  farmer found a newly born baby goat  he's named it miracle  i'm only worried about these animals if  i'd died it wouldn't matter  when our village was being evacuated i  couldn't leave i asked my parents  if we die here shall we die together  with these animals and they said yes  so we stayed i wish those animals  survived and i was dead  instead they are innocent  volunteers have joined the firefighters  working across the southern region  like college student rayhan in antalya's  executive district  all seniors in our village survive the  fire except for my 82 year old  grandfather  he got poisoned by the smoke while  trying to put out the fire  i don't want other seniors to die  tourists had to be moved from some of  the hotels in mula's popular district of  bodrum as the fire spread down the hill  towards the seashore  the government suspects arson but  experts believe  excessive heat and strong winds are  likely to cause  climate change is also a crucial factor  turkey saw devastating floods in its  northern black sea region earlier in  july  for many years the mediterranean has  never seen such dry weather as it has in  the last 20 days  meteorologists have actually warned  fires are unavoidable in the next 15  days and may continue until september  the fire which started in marmaris has  now spread to other locations  the government has been criticized for a  shortage of firefighting aircraft  azerbaijan iran russia and ukraine have  sent equipment and personnel  but turkey's forestry minister warns the  humidity level is going  down in the coming days which means more  attention  and measures are needed to put out the  fires in turkey's southern green hills  and ease the pain of those who have lost  everything  cinnamon solo al jazeera istanbul
 

